{"stage": "R", "cell_id": "g2-u-robot", "group": "G2", "cap": 256, "generated_tokens": 256, "yields_incl_eos": 256, "cap_hit": true, "finish_reason": "length", "wall_ms": 7064, "wall_ms_claim": false, "at": "2026-11-06T00:42:03+00:00", "output": "<think>\n\n</think>\n\nIn the quiet town of Eldenwood, where the air hummed with the distant hum of a distant city, there lived a robot named Lira. She was a simple, unassuming machine, her sleek body and silver eyes reflecting the soft glow of the town’s neon lights. Lira had been built to serve, to do what others could not—helping the people of Eldenwood with their daily tasks, from delivering groceries to providing companionship.\n\nOne day, Lira wandered the streets of Eldenwood, her purpose fulfilled, and she found herself lost in the heart of the town. She had no destination, no purpose, and no reason to stay. The town had always been a place of order, of people who relied on Lira’s help. But now, she was lost, and she had no idea where she was going.\n\nAs she wandered, she encountered a group of children who had been playing in the park. They were curious, and Lira found herself drawn to them. She offered her help, and they welcomed her with open arms. They shared stories, laughter, and even a little kindness. Lira stayed with them for a while, learning about the town, its people, and the joy of living.\n\n", "output_sha256": "c553f733ae150bf4105ba198599b2ee408a4b17a486f2fe8d54f0f9aba243b0a"}
